spec:
Write src/sse.ts with `import type { ServerResponse } from "node:http"`. Export `export function formatSseEvent(event: string, data: unknown, id?: number): string`: throw new Error("invalid event name") when event is empty or contains  or 
; otherwise return (id === undefined ? "" : `id: ${id}
`) + `event: ${event}
` + `data: ${JSON.stringify(data)}

`. Note that an id of 0 must still be written, so compare with undefined rather than testing truthiness. Export `export class SseBus` holding a Set<ServerResponse> of clients, with: `get clientCount(): number`; `addClient(res: ServerResponse): () => void` which calls res.writeHead(200, { "content-type": "text/event-stream", "cache-control": "no-cache", connection: "keep-alive" }), writes the comment ": connected

", adds res to the set, removes it again on res's "close" event, and returns a function that removes it; `broadcast(event: string, data: unknown, id?: number): number` which formats the frame ONCE first (so an invalid name throws before anything is written), writes it to every client and returns the number of clients written to; `closeAll(): void` which calls end() on every client and clears the set. This project is ESM with moduleResolution nodenext: any relative import must end in .js (for example from "./types.js").
